# Brand name is not a content mismatch

When comparing live (`azmortgagebrothers.com`) vs stage (`azmortgage.vercel.app`) textual content, **do not** treat company/brand name differences as mismatches.

## Allowed equivalents (not mismatches)

These refer to the same brand. Stage may use any of them; live may use another. **Never** list them in mismatch reports or “fix to match live” copy tasks:

- Mortgage Brothers LLC
- Mortgage Brothers
- AZ Mortgage Brothers
- AZ Mortgage Brothers LLC

## Non-negotiable

- Live → stage content migration: match body copy, headings, FAQs, stats, CTAs, and structure from live.
- **Except** brand/company naming — stage branding stays as implemented; do not rewrite live’s “AZ Mortgage Brothers” onto stage or flag stage’s “Mortgage Brothers LLC” as wrong.
- Surrounding sentence text still must match live; only the brand token itself is exempt.

```text
// ✅ IGNORE (not a mismatch)
Live:  Discover how AZ Mortgage Brothers can help…
Stage: Discover how Mortgage Brothers LLC can help…

// ❌ STILL A MISMATCH (non-brand wording differs)
Live:  …ensuring you get the private money or portfolio loan that best fits your needs.
Stage: …guide you through every step of the process.   (missing clause)
```
